class=\"citation no-link\">359 Pa. Super. 631</span>, <span class=\"citation no-link\">515 A. 2d 620</span>; No. 86-6470, <span class=\"citation multiple-matches\"><a href=\"/c/So.%202d/500/57/\">500 So. 2d 57</a></span>.</p>\n</opinion>"},{"id":9061345,"type":"dissent","typeCode":"040dissent","perCuriam":false,"author":"Brennanmarshall","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":657,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"dissent\">\n<author id=\"b935-15\">Justice Brennan and Justice Marshall,</author>\n<p id=\"A_8\">dissenting.</p>\n<p id=\"AC0Y\">Adhering to our views that the death penalty is in all circumstances cruel and unusual punishment prohibited by the Eighth and Fourteenth Amendments, <em>Gregg </em>v. <em>Georgia, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9426555\"><a href=\"/opinion/109532/gregg-v-georgia/#227\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Gregg v. Georgia\">428 U. S. 153, <page-number citation-index=\"1\" label=\"1008\">*1008</page-number>227, 231</a></span> (1976), we would grant certiorari and vacate the death sentences in these cases.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}